WEBVTT


00:02:26.558 --> 00:02:29.960
Martin.


00:02:29.995 --> 00:02:32.499
Come on, we're on.


00:02:39.604 --> 00:02:46.443
How do you
get by with so little sleep?


00:02:46.478 --> 00:02:48.309
Ambition, good diet.


00:02:48.344 --> 00:02:50.162
Constant self-medication.


00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:51.945
Time you got a new bag?


00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.514
I got this from
a friend of the family.


00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:56.320
- It used to be his.
- Oh, well, in that case...


00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.658
I kinda like it.


00:03:04.658 --> 00:03:06.026
You going to that thing
for the new residents?


00:03:06.061 --> 00:03:09.995
I don't know.


00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.897
Carson's daughter's gonna be there.


00:03:11.898 --> 00:03:11.934
Who's carson?


00:03:12.531 --> 00:03:14.333
Radiology.


00:03:14.368 --> 00:03:16.002
Supposedly his daughter's
a real peach.


00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:17.970
Come on, Martin,


00:03:18.005 --> 00:03:20.239
Time to start looking
for that trophy wife.


00:03:20.274 --> 00:03:22.592
Bring the bag.


00:03:22.627 --> 00:03:28.285
Dr. Levy, 4152.


00:03:33.285 --> 00:03:37.289
How are you...
Mr. Sanchez?


00:03:37.324 --> 00:03:38.555
No Hablo Ingles.


00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.556
Oh.


00:03:40.591 --> 00:03:43.527
- No Hablo Espanol.
- Doctor,


00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.468
Excuse me one... On moment.


00:03:53.503 --> 00:03:55.535
Por favor, doctor...


00:03:55.570 --> 00:04:00.008
Dr. Page?
Do you speak spanish?


00:04:00.043 --> 00:04:04.244
No.


00:04:04.279 --> 00:04:07.351
Can you cough?


00:04:07.386 --> 00:04:10.424
Thank you.


00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:18.992
Okay, you need a lot of rest.


00:04:19.027 --> 00:04:21.258
Rest. Sleep.


00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:23.712
You need to rest.


00:04:23.747 --> 00:04:25.923
- Yes.
That's what you need. Okay?


00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:27.846
The barium pictures were negative.


00:04:27.881 --> 00:04:29.700
Why the D-Xyclose
absorption series?


00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:33.639
I felt I should rule out
Zollinger-Ellison syndrome,


00:04:34.638 --> 00:04:36.472
Whipple's disease, and celiac.


00:04:36.507 --> 00:04:40.010
I say mild peptic ulcer.
I mean, possible chronic reflux.


00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:43.697
Smokes, drinks...
filed for divorce.


00:04:43.732 --> 00:04:47.350
I didn't know about the divorce.


00:04:47.385 --> 00:04:50.152
Did you talk to her?


00:04:50.187 --> 00:04:52.087
Not about stuff like that.


00:04:52.122 --> 00:04:54.457
We're not fishing
for syndromes here, folks.


00:04:54.492 --> 00:04:57.310
Communication is key.


00:04:57.345 --> 00:05:00.421
- Dr. Waylans.
- Yes?


00:05:00.456 --> 00:05:02.810
Ah. Martin...blake.


00:05:02.845 --> 00:05:05.131
Things going okay?


00:05:05.166 --> 00:05:07.232
Yeah. I was wondering,


00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:09.370
You did the infectious
diseases fellowship?


00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:10.337
Yeah.


00:05:10.372 --> 00:05:13.741
Well, I'm applying.
Do you have any advice?


00:05:13.776 --> 00:05:16.560
You're only six days
into residency.


00:05:16.595 --> 00:05:19.345
You can't even apply
till next year.


00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.531
I just want to be prepared.


00:05:21.566 --> 00:05:23.648
Oh. Well, it's not much.


00:05:23.683 --> 00:05:26.351
You know, a good candidate
is just a good doctor.


00:05:26.386 --> 00:05:28.285
Right.


00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.089
You do know the secret
to being a good doctor,


00:05:30.124 --> 00:05:31.555
Don't you, Martin?


00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.359
You act like one.


00:05:34.394 --> 00:05:37.193
I do, I think.


00:05:37.228 --> 00:05:39.897
Well, then, you're fine.


00:05:39.932 --> 00:05:42.531
- Dr. Waylans?
- Yes, Martin?


00:05:42.566 --> 00:05:44.667
Is it possible to get
our I.D. Picture retaken?


00:05:44.702 --> 00:05:48.771
I have no idea.


00:05:48.806 --> 00:05:51.574
Excuse me, what does that say?


00:05:51.609 --> 00:05:54.218
Penicillin.


00:06:03.217 --> 00:06:05.254
Excuse me, when will
the doctor be here?


00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:06.754
I am the doctor.


00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:09.625
Okay, that's it for now.


00:06:10.625 --> 00:06:13.525
Nurse?
I'll need labs drawn.


00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.596
You're gonna have to
do it yourself... We're swamped.


00:06:15.631 --> 00:06:16.696
You know how, right?


00:06:16.731 --> 00:06:21.379
Yes. Of course. Thank you.


00:06:33.378 --> 00:06:34.677
Is that okay?


00:06:34.712 --> 00:06:38.083
Sorry. A phlebotomist
is supposed to do this.


00:06:38.118 --> 00:06:39.248
A what?


00:06:39.283 --> 00:06:40.750
It's who draws the blood.


00:06:40.785 --> 00:06:42.730
Doctors aren't supposed
to have to do this.


00:06:53.729 --> 00:06:56.766
There you go.


00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:59.425
Okay.


00:08:05.161 --> 00:08:07.895
Here you are.


00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.899
I'm so sorry, I thought
you were someone else.


00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:13.533
Who did you think I was?


00:08:13.568 --> 00:08:14.701
I see you've met
my esteemed colleague.


00:08:14.736 --> 00:08:17.337
I did.


00:08:17.372 --> 00:08:17.639
For a minute,
I thought he was you.


00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:20.641
There's only one of me.
That's the rule.


00:08:20.676 --> 00:08:22.642
This is Martin.
Martin, this is christine.


00:08:22.677 --> 00:08:25.582
- Hi.
- Dr. Carson's daughter.


00:08:29.582 --> 00:08:31.884
So back to you being such
a big nerd in high school.


00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:33.351
- The biggest.
- Really?


00:08:33.386 --> 00:08:35.454
Yep. And then
one day I realized


00:08:35.489 --> 00:08:36.920
I was gonna die a virgin.


00:08:36.955 --> 00:08:39.425
That thought can come as quite
a shock to a young man.


00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:41.946
Don't you have some
other rooms to attend to?


00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.482
Let's just be a couple dirty
mexicans and make it happen.


00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.183
Make what happen?


00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:48.436
How 'bout I just talk to you?


00:09:48.471 --> 00:09:50.654
Let's make ourselves useful.


00:09:50.689 --> 00:09:52.657
Jimmy, come on.


00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:54.656
Yo.


00:09:54.691 --> 00:09:58.565
Good morning, doc.


00:10:01.565 --> 00:10:04.434
Hi.
How you feeling?


00:10:04.469 --> 00:10:06.601
Bad.


00:10:06.636 --> 00:10:07.603
What's wrong with me again?


00:10:08.603 --> 00:10:11.706
Pyelonephritis.


00:10:11.741 --> 00:10:13.844
It's a UTI of the upper tract
and kidney.


00:10:15.843 --> 00:10:22.917
Pie-Lo-Na-Fry-Tis.


00:10:22.952 --> 00:10:25.522
Like that?


00:10:28.522 --> 00:10:33.960
Pyelonephritis.
Mm-Hmm.


00:10:33.995 --> 00:10:35.762
Sit up.


00:10:35.797 --> 00:10:37.494
Okay...


00:10:37.529 --> 00:10:39.999
are you sore there?
- Yeah.


00:10:40.034 --> 00:10:41.318
Here?


00:10:41.353 --> 00:10:42.602
Yeah.


00:10:43.602 --> 00:10:47.838
Pyelonephritis.


00:10:47.873 --> 00:10:49.773
Can you die from that?


00:10:49.808 --> 00:10:51.910
Maybe, if you never
took care of it.


00:10:51.945 --> 00:10:53.978
But that's what us doctors
are here for.


00:10:54.013 --> 00:10:56.012
I thought you guys
just played golf.


00:10:56.047 --> 00:10:58.282
I don't know how to play golf.


00:10:58.317 --> 00:11:00.517
I thought all doctors
played golf.


00:11:00.552 --> 00:11:02.922
I'm gonna learn.


00:11:05.922 --> 00:11:07.055
Oh, hello, doctor.


00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:09.759
Doctor, nice to see you again.


00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:11.392
How's she doing?


00:11:11.427 --> 00:11:13.762
Good. Responding to
antibiotics.


00:11:13.797 --> 00:11:16.696
I could've died...right?


00:11:16.731 --> 00:11:18.616
I was just saying
it can be serious.


00:11:18.651 --> 00:11:20.465
But it's completely
under control.


00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.670
So you mean, like,
if this were before hospitals,


00:11:22.705 --> 00:11:23.670
She'd be dead?


00:11:23.705 --> 00:11:25.704
I didn't say that.


00:11:25.739 --> 00:11:28.109
It's amazing knowing how
to save people like that.


00:11:28.144 --> 00:11:29.576
I bet you even know
the name of this.


00:11:29.611 --> 00:11:30.942
Philtrum.


00:11:30.977 --> 00:11:32.579
See, I told you he'd know it.


00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.650
Hi.


00:11:40.685 --> 00:11:44.622
- Oh, hi, rich.
- Hey, Mrs. Nixon. Val.


00:11:44.657 --> 00:11:46.457
This is my doctor.


00:11:46.492 --> 00:11:48.461
He said I could have died.
- Dr. Blake.


00:11:48.496 --> 00:11:49.731
Hey.


00:11:52.731 --> 00:11:56.867
So...how's it going?


00:11:56.902 --> 00:11:58.033
Okay.


00:11:58.068 --> 00:12:00.069
You able to walk or...


00:12:00.104 --> 00:12:02.003
I'll look in again later on.


00:12:02.038 --> 00:12:04.741
You got, like,
some kind of infection?


00:12:04.776 --> 00:12:07.676
This says "penicillin," right?


00:12:07.711 --> 00:12:08.742
Yeah.


00:12:08.777 --> 00:12:10.096
Come with me, please.


00:12:28.094 --> 00:12:29.896
Mr. Sanchez is allergic
to penicillin.


00:12:29.931 --> 00:12:32.530
Well, it didn't say so
on the...


00:12:32.565 --> 00:12:34.735
This isn't the original admit
sheet... Where's the original?


00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.468
I don't know what
you're talking about.


00:12:36.503 --> 00:12:39.405
On the original sheet, it said
"NKA," no known allergies.


00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.672
- Well, did you ask him?
- He doesn't speak english.


00:12:41.707 --> 00:12:44.010
If you knew he was allergic,
why'd you give him penicillin?


00:12:44.045 --> 00:12:47.479
Because you're the doctor.
I only do what you say.


00:12:47.514 --> 00:12:48.581
Okay, let's get
a benadryl line...


00:12:49.581 --> 00:12:52.451
Already took care of it.
Thank you.


00:12:52.486 --> 00:12:53.450
Where are you going?


00:12:53.485 --> 00:12:53.585
To file an incident report.


00:12:54.585 --> 00:12:55.818
A what? Why?


00:12:55.853 --> 00:12:57.589
This is an incident.
It's procedure.


00:12:58.589 --> 00:13:03.161
And can you rewrite this
legibly?


00:13:03.196 --> 00:13:04.625
What are you doing?


00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.896
I'm looking for
the original admit sheet.


00:13:06.931 --> 00:13:08.029
I'm sorry, doctor,


00:13:08.064 --> 00:13:08.598
But whatever it is
you're looking for,


00:13:09.598 --> 00:13:10.832
You're not gonna find it there.


00:13:10.867 --> 00:13:13.736
Here you go, T.
Little present for you.


00:13:13.771 --> 00:13:15.881
Marty!


00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.985
This seat taken?


00:13:31.985 --> 00:13:32.784
Look, right, right, right...


00:13:32.819 --> 00:13:36.423
Look, look, look, look.
Hey, nancy,


00:13:36.458 --> 00:13:40.028
You want to sit down,
right here?


00:13:41.028 --> 00:13:44.594
So that's a no.


00:13:44.629 --> 00:13:47.834
Have a good weekend.


00:13:47.869 --> 00:13:50.535
Excuse me.


00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.575
Excuse me a second.
- No problem.


00:13:57.575 --> 00:13:59.678
Dr. Waylans, can I talk
to you for a second?


00:13:59.713 --> 00:14:03.149
Sure.


00:14:05.149 --> 00:14:07.518
I just wanted to ask you
about incident reports.


00:14:07.553 --> 00:14:09.653
Is this about
the sanchez thing?


00:14:09.688 --> 00:14:10.918
I wouldn't worry about it.


00:14:10.953 --> 00:14:13.606
But does it go on my record?
I mean, is it bad?


00:14:13.641 --> 00:14:16.259
I don't think so.
I mean, it's not good.


00:14:16.294 --> 00:14:19.160
Will it affect my application


00:14:19.195 --> 00:14:21.130
For the infectious diseases
fellowship?


00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.757
I can't undo it,
if that's what you mean.


00:15:30.791 --> 00:15:33.627
I haven't heard that before.


00:15:33.662 --> 00:15:36.028
No, that's fine. Perfect.


00:15:36.063 --> 00:15:37.898
While you're at it,
why don't you just go screw her


00:15:37.933 --> 00:15:39.697
And get it over with?


00:15:39.732 --> 00:15:42.635
No. Because I'm sick,
and I'm in the hospital,


00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.069
If you haven't noticed.


00:15:44.104 --> 00:15:48.640
Oh, please.
You're such an asshole!


00:15:48.675 --> 00:15:52.844
Go to hell.


00:15:52.879 --> 00:15:55.847
I'm getting better.


00:15:55.882 --> 00:15:58.483
It looks that way.


00:15:58.518 --> 00:16:01.050
Everything okay?


00:16:01.085 --> 00:16:03.986
Do you remember rich?


00:16:04.021 --> 00:16:05.590
I should break up with him.


00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.659
You think I should
break up with him?


00:16:08.694 --> 00:16:10.927
That's none of my business.


00:16:10.962 --> 00:16:13.796
He is the most popular guy
in school.


00:16:13.831 --> 00:16:16.632
I wasn't the most popular guy
in school.


00:16:16.667 --> 00:16:21.669
And now I'm a doctor.


00:16:21.704 --> 00:16:24.273
What do you think rich
is going to be?


00:16:24.308 --> 00:16:27.141
I don't know.


00:16:27.176 --> 00:16:29.609
An idiot.


00:16:29.644 --> 00:16:31.446
It's hard to dump him, though.


00:16:31.481 --> 00:16:33.212
We've been together
for a while.


00:16:33.247 --> 00:16:35.249
I mean, I don't know
if we're in love or anything.


00:16:35.284 --> 00:16:39.537
- Well, you know what they say.
- What?


00:16:39.572 --> 00:16:43.790
If you love someone...
set them free.


00:16:43.825 --> 00:16:45.056
Who says that?


00:16:45.091 --> 00:16:47.094
Sting.


00:16:47.129 --> 00:16:49.096
I think.


00:16:49.131 --> 00:16:51.028
Who?


00:16:51.063 --> 00:16:53.385
Excuse me, doctor.


00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.707
I'm with a patient.


00:17:01.706 --> 00:17:05.118
I can't do these orders
until I can read them.


00:17:13.117 --> 00:17:16.853
I can't do these orders...


00:17:16.888 --> 00:17:21.224
press "door open".
Press "door open"!


00:17:26.963 --> 00:17:30.831
Hello, doctor.


00:17:30.866 --> 00:17:33.668
Having a rough day, are we?


00:17:33.703 --> 00:17:35.669
No. Fine.


00:17:35.704 --> 00:17:37.455
Don't worry, I got it too.


00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.170
Every goddamn day's
a shit fight


00:17:39.205 --> 00:17:41.412
Just to get out of bed
in the morning.


00:17:44.412 --> 00:17:48.146
Oh.


00:17:48.181 --> 00:17:50.133
What's bugging you, doc?


00:17:50.168 --> 00:17:52.050
This is a hospital.


00:17:52.085 --> 00:17:53.953
The staff is supposed
to follow orders, right?


00:17:53.988 --> 00:17:55.355
Isn't that how
it's supposed to be?


00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.857
Doctors get a little respect?


00:17:57.892 --> 00:18:00.290
Uh, I don't know.
Maybe.


00:18:00.325 --> 00:18:03.159
It's probably not
what you think, though.


00:18:03.194 --> 00:18:05.967
I just want things to be
like they're supposed to be.


00:18:08.966 --> 00:18:11.166
How long has theresa been here?


00:18:11.201 --> 00:18:13.237
Didn't you learn how
to get rid of people like that


00:18:13.272 --> 00:18:14.236
In med school?


00:18:14.271 --> 00:18:16.238
Just slip 'em something,


00:18:16.273 --> 00:18:18.941
Then they're going along,
and then bam!


00:18:18.976 --> 00:18:20.877
Heart attack! Too bad.


00:18:22.914 --> 00:18:24.812
I'm kidding, doc.


00:18:24.847 --> 00:18:28.085
Just, uh...bet you were
thinking about it.


00:18:30.085 --> 00:18:31.914
Okay, I'm clocking out.


00:18:54.741 --> 00:18:56.306
Hi.


00:18:56.341 --> 00:18:59.745
Hi.
How are you feeling?


00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.381
Okay, I guess.


00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.986
What was the deal
with that nurse?


00:19:08.986 --> 00:19:10.904
It was a misunderstanding.
It's okay.


00:19:10.939 --> 00:19:12.822
Shouldn't she be fired
or something


00:19:12.857 --> 00:19:14.157
For yelling at a doctor?


00:19:14.192 --> 00:19:16.758
Probably.


00:19:16.793 --> 00:19:19.530
I don't want to cause a fuss.


00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.532
Am I cured?


00:19:22.567 --> 00:19:24.536
Nearly.


00:19:26.536 --> 00:19:28.771
No more hospital?


00:19:28.806 --> 00:19:30.405
No.


00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.816
No more helpful advice?


00:19:40.816 --> 00:19:45.318
I'll tell nurse Ratched
you're a good doctor.


00:19:45.353 --> 00:19:47.822
Maybe she'll leave you alone.


00:19:47.857 --> 00:19:48.556
Thanks.


00:19:49.556 --> 00:19:51.897
You're a good patient.


00:20:13.011 --> 00:20:15.547
Ah, Nixon.
Signs are okay.


00:20:16.547 --> 00:20:19.817
No pain, no spikes.
She's outta here.


00:20:19.852 --> 00:20:21.784
Just another day, to be sure?


00:20:21.819 --> 00:20:24.821
I already signed her out.
Let's move on.


00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:27.456
Mr. Sanchez...


00:20:35.231 --> 00:20:37.333
Hi.
Are you Diane's doctor?


00:20:37.368 --> 00:20:39.468
- Yes.
- I'm Diane's father.


00:20:39.503 --> 00:20:41.534
Thank you for everything.


00:20:41.569 --> 00:20:44.070
I was just coming
to say good-Bye.


00:20:44.105 --> 00:20:46.040
My wife just took her
down to the car.


00:20:46.075 --> 00:20:48.474
Any last-Minute advice?


00:20:48.509 --> 00:20:50.476
Finish her pills.
She could relapse.


00:20:50.511 --> 00:20:52.143
Okay, we'll do that.


00:20:52.178 --> 00:20:53.445
Uh, I don't know
how to say this,


00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.466
But my daughter took
quite a shine to you.


00:20:56.501 --> 00:20:58.976
She thought you two
got on pretty well,


00:20:59.011 --> 00:21:01.453
And she wondered if
I might ask you over


00:21:01.488 --> 00:21:04.523
For dinner on friday.


00:21:04.558 --> 00:21:07.309
Friday. Yes.


00:21:07.344 --> 00:21:09.353
That'd be nice.


00:21:09.388 --> 00:21:11.376
- Great.
- Friday.


00:21:11.411 --> 00:21:13.329
We'll count on it.


00:21:13.364 --> 00:21:15.890
See you then.
8:00 friday.


00:21:38.888 --> 00:21:40.556
Diane, you feeling better?


00:21:41.556 --> 00:21:44.958
How are you feeling?


00:21:44.993 --> 00:21:48.362
Mr. Nixon, Mrs. Nixon.


00:21:53.567 --> 00:21:56.520
- Is that the doctor?
- Uh, yeah.


00:21:56.555 --> 00:21:59.473
- Let him in.
- Hi. Hi. Come on in.


00:21:59.508 --> 00:22:01.909
Welcome to our home.


00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:06.579
Oh, you remember valerie,
right?


00:22:06.614 --> 00:22:08.380
Hi.
I love your jacket.


00:22:08.415 --> 00:22:10.247
Thanks.


00:22:10.282 --> 00:22:11.550
And this is our youngest,
donny.


00:22:12.549 --> 00:22:15.084
- Hello.
- What's up?


00:22:15.119 --> 00:22:17.626
- Not much.
- Please sit down.


00:22:21.626 --> 00:22:22.893
Where's diane?


00:22:22.928 --> 00:22:24.126
Oh, she's out.


00:22:24.161 --> 00:22:26.427
I told her to stay...


00:22:26.462 --> 00:22:29.032
so that she didn't seem
ungrateful...


00:22:29.067 --> 00:22:30.299
because we really are.


00:22:30.334 --> 00:22:36.509
But...she's having a talk
with rich.


00:22:40.509 --> 00:22:43.175
So what's it like
being a doctor?


00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:46.347
A lot of work.
A lot of responsibility.


00:22:46.382 --> 00:22:48.948
But I like it.


00:22:48.983 --> 00:22:50.584
How many operations
you do a week?


00:22:50.619 --> 00:22:52.585
I'm in internal medicine.


00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:54.055
What's that, like, intestines?


00:22:54.090 --> 00:22:55.354
Donny, not at the table.


00:22:55.389 --> 00:22:57.324
That'd be great. Get in there
and just dig around.


00:22:57.359 --> 00:23:00.925
I don't do surgery.


00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:04.064
I bet it pays pretty well,
doesn't it, being a doctor?


00:23:04.099 --> 00:23:07.933
Donny, don't pry.


00:23:07.968 --> 00:23:09.232
It's actually less
than you think,


00:23:09.267 --> 00:23:11.437
But it's a lot more
than I'd make back home.


00:23:11.472 --> 00:23:12.538
And he makes more
than you do, donny.


00:23:13.538 --> 00:23:15.207
Besides,
the money comes when you go


00:23:15.242 --> 00:23:17.514
Into private practice, right?


00:23:22.513 --> 00:23:24.782
You got a nice place?


00:23:24.817 --> 00:23:26.651
It's okay.
The beach.


00:23:26.686 --> 00:23:28.484
Oh, I love the beach.


00:23:28.519 --> 00:23:30.052
You're so lucky.


00:23:30.087 --> 00:23:30.952
I wish I lived by the beach


00:23:30.987 --> 00:23:32.489
And knew all this
incredible knowledge


00:23:32.524 --> 00:23:33.523
About the human body.


00:23:34.523 --> 00:23:36.459
You know plenty.


00:23:36.494 --> 00:23:38.394
Donny, you pig!


00:23:38.429 --> 00:23:39.526
Stop...


00:23:39.561 --> 00:23:41.329
- Valerie!
- Mom!


00:23:41.364 --> 00:23:43.063
He started it.


00:23:43.098 --> 00:23:45.099
Mom, this was brand-New.


00:23:45.134 --> 00:23:47.635
You're just gonna get sperm
on it anyway.


00:23:48.536 --> 00:23:50.105
Let's not have that kind
of language


00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:51.673
At the table there, guy.


00:23:51.708 --> 00:23:54.226
Honestly, donny.


00:23:54.261 --> 00:23:56.708
I am so sorry, doctor.


00:23:56.743 --> 00:24:00.545
It's okay.


00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:03.349
Could I use your restroom?
- Certainly.


00:24:03.384 --> 00:24:04.484
It's down the hall
on the right.


00:24:04.519 --> 00:24:05.616
Excuse me.


00:24:05.651 --> 00:24:07.217
What, mom?
He's a doctor.


00:24:07.252 --> 00:24:08.387
It's not like he's never
heard of sperm before.


00:24:08.422 --> 00:24:10.890
- Hey!
- You are upsetting your father.


00:24:10.925 --> 00:24:13.358
Where do you come up
with this stuff?


00:24:13.393 --> 00:24:14.815
Oh!


00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:16.237
Sorry.


00:25:35.798 --> 00:25:37.835
It's just something
came up at the hospital,


00:25:37.870 --> 00:25:40.273
And I really have to go.


00:25:40.308 --> 00:25:42.678
- Bye.
- Thank you.


00:26:54.336 --> 00:26:57.739
Okay, that's it.
Have a good day, everyone.


00:26:57.774 --> 00:27:01.573
Thanks.
I'll see you there.


00:27:01.608 --> 00:27:05.578
Blake, can you stay
for a second, please?


00:27:05.613 --> 00:27:08.518
Sure.


00:27:11.518 --> 00:27:12.723
Have a seat.


00:27:17.722 --> 00:27:20.793
So...how's it going?


00:27:20.828 --> 00:27:23.161
Fine.


00:27:23.196 --> 00:27:26.264
Oh, yeah? Tired?


00:27:26.299 --> 00:27:29.284
A little.


00:27:29.319 --> 00:27:32.234
Happy?


00:27:32.269 --> 00:27:33.606
Want some coffee?


00:27:36.606 --> 00:27:37.640
No, thanks.


00:27:37.675 --> 00:27:41.579
First year of residency
can be tough, I know.


00:27:41.614 --> 00:27:43.344
If this is about
Mr. Sanchez...


00:27:43.379 --> 00:27:47.483
I just wanted to chat
about the big picture.


00:27:47.518 --> 00:27:49.416
Tell me something, Martin...


00:27:49.451 --> 00:27:51.321
When did you first want
to become a doctor?


00:27:51.356 --> 00:27:52.419
When?


00:27:52.454 --> 00:27:55.456
- Yeah.
- A long time ago, I guess.


00:27:55.491 --> 00:27:58.944
Did you know why?


00:27:58.979 --> 00:28:02.361
Why? Because...


00:28:02.396 --> 00:28:03.664
a friend of my mother's
was a doctor,


00:28:03.699 --> 00:28:05.363
And he was respected,


00:28:05.398 --> 00:28:06.501
And I guess I just always
thought, you know,


00:28:07.501 --> 00:28:11.471
To have that respect, and to...


00:28:11.506 --> 00:28:13.572
and be helping people.


00:28:15.608 --> 00:28:17.577
Yeah, people go into medicine
for all kinds of reasons.


00:28:17.612 --> 00:28:19.546
You know, sometimes
they don't really think about it


00:28:19.581 --> 00:28:21.645
Till they're here,
face-To-Face with it all.


00:28:21.680 --> 00:28:24.616
And sometimes they realize
the stress and the hours


00:28:24.651 --> 00:28:26.617
And the nature of the work


00:28:26.652 --> 00:28:28.385
Aren't what they thought
it would be.


00:28:28.420 --> 00:28:30.537
I mean, it's not unusual
for people to realize


00:28:30.572 --> 00:28:32.656
Maybe this isn't what
they wanted after all.


00:28:32.691 --> 00:28:33.755
This is what I want.


00:28:33.790 --> 00:28:35.290
I mean, I know I can do better.


00:28:35.492 --> 00:28:37.510
It's just taking time for me
to learn your system here.


00:28:37.545 --> 00:28:39.528
I mean, I didn't have
all the advantages, you know,


00:28:39.563 --> 00:28:41.581
Growing up and school,
and so sometimes


00:28:41.616 --> 00:28:43.599
I just have to work harder,
and I do.


00:28:43.634 --> 00:28:45.567
Some of the nurses, I mean...


00:28:45.602 --> 00:28:46.503
Maryanne's fine,
but with theresa...


00:28:47.503 --> 00:28:48.506
I double-Majored
in chemistry and biology.


00:28:49.505 --> 00:28:50.870
I went to school,
I did all this work,


00:28:50.905 --> 00:28:53.409
And she just treats me
like I'm some nobody.


00:28:53.444 --> 00:28:56.879
It doesn't seem fair, but...


00:28:56.914 --> 00:28:58.583
I do want this.


00:29:04.486 --> 00:29:08.656
There you go.
- Thanks.


00:29:40.583 --> 00:29:42.884
Hi, Martin, it's Valerie Nixon.


00:29:42.919 --> 00:29:44.688
It was really nice to see you
the other night.


00:29:44.723 --> 00:29:46.854
I'm sorry you had to rush off.


00:29:46.889 --> 00:29:49.792
My mom actually got you
a gift basket,


00:29:49.827 --> 00:29:51.493
But we forgot
to give it to you.


00:29:51.528 --> 00:29:53.430
So I don't know if you wanted
to arrange a time


00:29:53.465 --> 00:29:54.263
To come by and get it,


00:29:54.298 --> 00:29:57.433
Or I could drop it by
the hospital...


00:29:57.468 --> 00:29:59.401
or your apartment, if you like.


00:29:59.436 --> 00:30:00.900
So give us a call.


00:30:00.935 --> 00:30:02.435
I'm home any time but tonight.


00:30:02.503 --> 00:30:06.122
Okay, bye.


00:30:53.148 --> 00:30:56.452
Oh, dr. Blake, come in.


00:30:56.487 --> 00:30:58.052
Thank you.


00:30:58.087 --> 00:31:00.022
Can I get you some coffee
or anything?


00:31:00.057 --> 00:31:01.087
No thanks.
Valerie called.


00:31:01.122 --> 00:31:03.558
She mentioned there was
something for me to collect?


00:31:03.593 --> 00:31:04.591
Yeah.


00:31:04.626 --> 00:31:05.961
But I'm expected
at the hospital.


00:31:05.996 --> 00:31:07.427
Oh, of course.


00:31:07.462 --> 00:31:08.964
Could I use your restroom?


00:31:08.999 --> 00:31:10.529
Certainly.


00:31:10.564 --> 00:31:12.591
You remember where it was?
- Yeah.


00:32:21.128 --> 00:32:25.197
- Oh, here you go.
- Thank you.


00:32:25.232 --> 00:32:27.632
It's just a little something
to say thanks.


00:32:27.667 --> 00:32:29.467
Thanks again, doctor.


00:32:29.502 --> 00:32:32.571
Any special instructions
for diane?


00:32:32.606 --> 00:32:35.176
Just finish her medicine.


00:32:37.175 --> 00:32:39.642
I thought it was just malaise


00:32:39.677 --> 00:32:42.280
From hanging around
the house so much.


00:32:42.315 --> 00:32:44.883
- I told you,
it's Pyelonephritis.


00:32:44.918 --> 00:32:46.649
Ow.


00:32:46.684 --> 00:32:51.120
I thought she was all better.


00:32:51.155 --> 00:32:54.988
It did seem that way.


00:32:55.023 --> 00:32:57.810
We'll run some tests
to make sure.


00:32:57.845 --> 00:33:00.597
But there are some
resistant strains


00:33:00.632 --> 00:33:02.936
That are harder to treat.


00:33:07.935 --> 00:33:10.710
Hey, doc!


00:33:14.709 --> 00:33:16.510
Hey, it's nice to have
the little number back


00:33:16.545 --> 00:33:18.610
In 324, huh?


00:33:18.645 --> 00:33:19.912
I don't think it's appropriate


00:33:19.947 --> 00:33:21.949
To talk about the patients
in that manner.


00:33:21.984 --> 00:33:24.249
Oh, yeah, yeah.


00:33:24.284 --> 00:33:27.219
Hippocratichyppocratic
oath, right? Yeah.


00:33:27.254 --> 00:33:28.854
I need a cam profile.


00:33:28.889 --> 00:33:31.624
- We need the ultrasound.
- Get it from...


00:33:31.659 --> 00:33:33.223
- There's one here.
- All right.


00:33:33.258 --> 00:33:36.629
Who's the primary doctor?
Where's the chart?


00:33:36.664 --> 00:33:39.181
What is this?
This doesn't make sense.


00:33:39.216 --> 00:33:41.699
Another allergic
reaction, doctor?


00:33:41.734 --> 00:33:44.671
No.
This is something else.


00:33:47.671 --> 00:33:49.538
See? Vancomycin.


00:33:49.573 --> 00:33:52.642
Not a penicillin reaction.
It wasn't my mistake.


00:33:52.677 --> 00:33:54.311
Yeah, looks like
red man syndrome.


00:33:54.346 --> 00:33:56.077
Well, that can happen when...


00:33:56.112 --> 00:33:57.848
When someone misadministers
Vancomycin.


00:33:57.883 --> 00:33:59.047
Which doesn't surprise me


00:33:59.082 --> 00:34:01.082
Because I never thought that
theresa, beyond her attitude,


00:34:01.117 --> 00:34:02.952
Was all that sharp
about these things.


00:34:02.987 --> 00:34:05.471
Well, I'll look into it.


00:34:05.506 --> 00:34:07.921
How's everything else?


00:34:07.956 --> 00:34:10.857
I see the Nixon girl is back?


00:34:10.892 --> 00:34:14.560
Yeah. She said she took
her oral meds.


00:34:14.595 --> 00:34:17.031
But I'll do a resistance culture
just to be sure.


00:34:17.066 --> 00:34:20.349
All right.
Keep up the good work.


00:34:35.348 --> 00:34:39.150
So...
can't keep away.


00:34:39.185 --> 00:34:40.659
It seems that way.


00:34:48.658 --> 00:34:51.010
I'm sorry.


00:34:51.045 --> 00:34:53.328
I'm not.


00:34:53.363 --> 00:34:55.672
You don't want to
go back to school?


00:35:01.671 --> 00:35:02.844
Rich?


00:35:07.843 --> 00:35:10.886
The medicine you're on now
is much stronger.


00:35:17.885 --> 00:35:19.820
You'll get better very soon.


00:35:19.855 --> 00:35:22.066
Do I have to?


00:38:07.202 --> 00:38:08.303
Ooh!


00:38:08.338 --> 00:38:09.539
Oh, I'm really so sorry,
doctor.


00:38:09.574 --> 00:38:10.441
- Excuse me.
- Sorry.


00:38:11.441 --> 00:38:11.441
Maryanne, I'm really busy...


00:38:12.409 --> 00:38:14.210
You know what, um...
they just let me go.


00:38:14.245 --> 00:38:16.679
And before you hear it
from anyone else,


00:38:16.714 --> 00:38:19.079
I messed up
Mr. Sanchez's Vancomycin.


00:38:19.114 --> 00:38:22.283
I switched the sheet,
and I just panicked.


00:38:22.318 --> 00:38:25.452
I'm just sorry
if I jeopardized a patient.


00:38:25.487 --> 00:38:26.852
I thought it was theresa.


00:38:26.887 --> 00:38:29.323
No. She didn't know
anything about it.


00:38:29.358 --> 00:38:31.491
Oh...


00:38:31.526 --> 00:38:33.564
so sorry to hold you up.


00:38:37.563 --> 00:38:40.201
It's fine.
Excuse me.


00:38:41.201 --> 00:38:42.898
Sorry, doctor.


00:39:12.894 --> 00:39:18.865
Good morning.


00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:22.272
How are you feeling?
- The same, I guess.


00:39:24.272 --> 00:39:26.373
Your temperature's up a little.


00:39:26.408 --> 00:39:28.174
Is that bad?


00:39:28.209 --> 00:39:29.976
It's nothing serious,


00:39:30.011 --> 00:39:32.847
But you might have to stay
an extra day or two.


00:39:32.882 --> 00:39:35.080
Is that bad?


00:39:35.115 --> 00:39:36.548
No. That's fine.


00:39:36.583 --> 00:39:40.097
Once you check in on me.


00:40:07.511 --> 00:40:09.579
- Someone's coming.
- What are you talking about?


00:40:14.383 --> 00:40:16.419
Oh, hey, doc.


00:40:17.419 --> 00:40:18.421
Uh...
- Get off me.


00:40:19.420 --> 00:40:22.224
We were just talking.


00:40:25.226 --> 00:40:27.227
Is this woman under sedation?


00:40:27.262 --> 00:40:29.564
It's cool, man.
It's just a party, man.


00:40:29.599 --> 00:40:32.498
Shit, it was her idea anyway.


00:40:32.533 --> 00:40:35.403
Mandy, tell the doctor
you're okay.


00:40:35.438 --> 00:40:38.438
Doctor, I'm okay.


00:40:44.210 --> 00:40:48.578
What are you doing
down here, doc?


00:40:48.613 --> 00:40:50.515
Is there something
I could help you with?


00:40:50.550 --> 00:40:53.431
Just get her out of here.


00:41:06.429 --> 00:41:08.498
All right, let's get you
back to bed now, mandy.


00:41:08.533 --> 00:41:11.000
Mm-Hmm.


00:41:11.035 --> 00:41:12.534
Nice work, doc.


00:41:12.569 --> 00:41:15.121
Son of a bitch.


00:41:50.670 --> 00:41:53.622
Weren't you off at midnight?


00:41:53.657 --> 00:41:56.905
Yes. I just had
some things to finish.


00:41:56.940 --> 00:42:00.153
This patient's been
a difficult case.


00:42:08.152 --> 00:42:09.619
Everything okay?


00:42:09.654 --> 00:42:12.320
Yeah, everything's fine.


00:42:12.355 --> 00:42:14.711
Why don't you go home, doctor.


00:43:44.705 --> 00:43:46.939
My biggest concern
would be an abscess


00:43:46.974 --> 00:43:49.175
Or some kind of resistant
bacterial strain.


00:43:49.210 --> 00:43:50.809
An abscess is doubtful.


00:43:50.844 --> 00:43:52.845
Keep your eye
on the resistance culture.


00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:54.797
We are seeing
more resistance in these.


00:43:54.832 --> 00:43:57.024
I was gonna start her
on Ceftazidime.


00:43:57.059 --> 00:43:59.218
Well, if she doesn't
start stabilizing,


00:43:59.253 --> 00:44:00.518
We're gonna have to move her
to icu.


00:44:00.553 --> 00:44:01.687
And keep an eye out for sepsis.


00:44:01.722 --> 00:44:02.821
How often are you
checking signs?


00:44:02.856 --> 00:44:04.755
- Two hours.
- Okay. Good.


00:44:04.790 --> 00:44:06.291
Let me know what
the resistance culture says.


00:44:06.326 --> 00:44:07.457
I will.


00:44:07.492 --> 00:44:11.394
What does that mean?


00:44:11.429 --> 00:44:13.130
Your infection
might be a little tougher


00:44:13.165 --> 00:44:14.367
Than we thought.


00:44:21.437 --> 00:44:23.137
We're starting you
on another antibiotic,


00:44:23.172 --> 00:44:24.840
And we need to make sure that
you're not developing sepsis.


00:44:24.875 --> 00:44:26.573
What's that?


00:44:26.608 --> 00:44:28.443
An intravascular infection.


00:44:28.478 --> 00:44:30.143
An intra what?


00:44:30.178 --> 00:44:33.349
It's in the bloodstream.


00:44:33.384 --> 00:44:34.549
Is that serious?


00:44:34.584 --> 00:44:36.487
It can be.


00:44:39.487 --> 00:44:43.859
I didn't think doctors
had to do that.


00:44:45.859 --> 00:44:48.493
I don't mind.


00:44:48.528 --> 00:44:52.764
If I have an operation,
will you operate on me?


00:44:52.799 --> 00:44:54.867
I don't operate.


00:44:54.902 --> 00:44:56.607
Hmm.


00:45:00.607 --> 00:45:03.139
I don't want to
cut into people.


00:45:03.174 --> 00:45:06.544
That's why I went
into internal medicine.


00:45:06.579 --> 00:45:08.145
If I do my job right,


00:45:08.180 --> 00:45:11.019
We never have to go in at all.


00:45:21.857 --> 00:45:23.627
I don't want to talk to him.


00:45:23.662 --> 00:45:25.531
Well, don't...


00:45:28.531 --> 00:45:30.238
think about it too much.


00:45:35.237 --> 00:45:36.838
You need rest.


00:45:36.873 --> 00:45:38.677
I know.


00:45:42.676 --> 00:45:43.842
Can I help you?


00:45:43.877 --> 00:45:46.546
Yeah, I'm, uh,
looking for Diane Nixon.


00:45:46.581 --> 00:45:48.883
I'm afraid
she can't take visitors.


00:45:48.918 --> 00:45:50.734
Look, man,
we had this big bust-Up.


00:45:50.769 --> 00:45:52.552
I just need to see her
for two minutes.


00:45:52.587 --> 00:45:53.453
It's not a good idea.


00:45:53.488 --> 00:45:55.289
Just leave her alone
for a little while.


00:45:55.324 --> 00:45:57.195
She needs rest.


00:46:02.194 --> 00:46:04.730
Give this to her.


00:46:04.765 --> 00:46:07.478
Sure.


00:47:03.583 --> 00:47:05.384
You should be sleeping.


00:47:06.384 --> 00:47:08.558
I can't.


00:47:13.558 --> 00:47:15.624
What did the expert say?


00:47:15.659 --> 00:47:17.761
He said it's a difficult case,


00:47:17.796 --> 00:47:19.863
But we're gonna
work together on it,


00:47:19.898 --> 00:47:23.801
And everything's gonna be okay.


00:47:25.801 --> 00:47:30.372
There's something
I didn't tell you...


00:47:30.407 --> 00:47:34.908
about before I came back
to the hospital.


00:47:34.943 --> 00:47:38.555
I don't know if it's what could
have made me get sick again.


00:47:47.554 --> 00:47:50.624
What's that?


00:47:50.659 --> 00:47:54.394
I had sex with rich
before I finished my medication.


00:47:54.429 --> 00:47:58.031
That can upset
your urinary tract, right?


00:47:58.066 --> 00:48:02.267
I don't think
that's what did it.


00:48:02.302 --> 00:48:05.674
I didn't think
you two were goin' out anymore.


00:48:07.674 --> 00:48:10.509
You know how sometimes you do
things you know you shouldn't,


00:48:10.544 --> 00:48:13.511
But you just can't help it?


00:48:13.546 --> 00:48:15.612
Yeah.


00:48:15.647 --> 00:48:18.917
I'm not gonna die, am I?


00:48:18.952 --> 00:48:22.984
No, of course not.


00:48:23.019 --> 00:48:30.326
I always thought if I was
gonna die, I wanted to, like,


00:48:30.361 --> 00:48:33.437
Get shot stopping a crime,
or something.


00:48:41.436 --> 00:48:44.546
I know that's stupid.


00:48:51.545 --> 00:48:54.449
Do you ever think about
stuff like that?


00:48:54.484 --> 00:48:58.485
When I was younger, maybe.


00:48:58.520 --> 00:49:00.951
It's silly.


00:49:00.986 --> 00:49:03.855
What did you imagine?


00:49:03.890 --> 00:49:07.026
I would think about
just walking into the ocean,


00:49:07.061 --> 00:49:10.096
And just disappearing,
like I never existed,


00:49:10.131 --> 00:49:13.132
And the world would just
go on without me.


00:49:13.167 --> 00:49:17.526
I love the ocean.


00:49:42.524 --> 00:49:45.394
I'm not sure I've seen
anything quite like this.


00:49:45.429 --> 00:49:47.126
Yeah, it's, uh,
been a tough case.


00:49:47.161 --> 00:49:50.014
They had an Acinetobacter
at south east general,


00:49:50.049 --> 00:49:52.867
But I've never seen one of these
so resistant before.


00:49:52.902 --> 00:49:54.501
You've been doing
regular cultures


00:49:54.536 --> 00:49:57.605
To check against some other bug,
maybe some nosocomial thing?


00:49:57.640 --> 00:49:58.670
I considered that,


00:49:58.705 --> 00:50:00.774
But nothing's
come up in cultures.


00:50:00.809 --> 00:50:02.808
Martin's been very thorough.


00:50:02.843 --> 00:50:04.809
He's done everything
I would have done.


00:50:04.844 --> 00:50:07.679
And she's been
properly administered all along?


00:50:07.714 --> 00:50:09.546
Yes.


00:50:09.581 --> 00:50:11.548
Well, Martin, it looks like


00:50:11.583 --> 00:50:17.454
You've landed yourself
a tricky one.


00:50:17.489 --> 00:50:21.560
I drew up the protocol
to treat the sepsis...


00:50:21.595 --> 00:50:24.079
Shoot.
I must have left it in my car.


00:50:24.114 --> 00:50:26.529
I'm due upstairs.
Would you mind?


00:50:26.564 --> 00:50:29.049
No. No, I was
just about to grab lunch.


00:50:29.084 --> 00:50:31.535
Silver mercedes,
johns hopkins stickers.


00:50:31.570 --> 00:50:34.269
And it's in the back.


00:51:53.075 --> 00:51:55.543
It's a tube
that goes into your heart.


00:51:55.578 --> 00:51:57.077
It doesn't hurt.


00:51:57.112 --> 00:52:00.080
So you can look in
any time you want?


00:52:00.115 --> 00:52:03.553
Yeah.


00:52:05.553 --> 00:52:09.340
If you had one, too,
we could have a heart-To-Heart.


00:53:33.331 --> 00:53:37.232
Hi.


00:53:37.267 --> 00:53:40.037
How are you feeling?


00:53:40.072 --> 00:53:43.204
Okay.


00:53:43.239 --> 00:53:45.840
Just kind of groggy.


00:53:45.875 --> 00:53:51.014
They put pain medicine
into your I.V.


00:53:51.049 --> 00:53:53.179
Any pain from the catheter?


00:53:53.214 --> 00:53:58.627
No. It's weird.
I feel kinda nice, actually.


00:54:05.626 --> 00:54:07.962
Can I ask you a question?


00:54:07.997 --> 00:54:10.267
Of course.


00:54:14.267 --> 00:54:19.775
You're not married or don't
have a girlfriend or anything.


00:54:22.775 --> 00:54:25.811
What's the question?


00:54:25.846 --> 00:54:29.679
Why not?


00:54:29.714 --> 00:54:33.321
You know how people are
in the world.


00:54:37.321 --> 00:54:40.159
Yeah.


00:54:43.159 --> 00:54:48.071
You know, for a while
I thought you liked my sister.


00:54:55.071 --> 00:54:56.975
No.


00:54:58.974 --> 00:55:05.079
Good, she's a slut.
You don't want a girl like that.


00:56:12.072 --> 00:56:15.118
Doctor.


00:56:31.189 --> 00:56:32.524
I know, I did it myself...


00:56:32.559 --> 00:56:34.009
Where is she?


00:56:34.044 --> 00:56:35.719
Excuse me.
Who?


00:56:35.754 --> 00:56:37.360
Diane...Nixon.


00:56:37.395 --> 00:56:39.029
Oh, they took her
for an M.R.I.


00:56:39.064 --> 00:56:40.262
I just got a code four.


00:56:40.297 --> 00:56:42.265
I don't know
what you're talking about.


00:56:42.300 --> 00:56:44.300
Where is she?


00:57:27.397 --> 00:57:30.318
- Charge.
- Clear!


00:57:58.868 --> 00:58:00.964
- clear!
- Clear!


00:58:28.961 --> 00:58:35.034
Yeah.
Yeah, that's it. Call it.


01:00:17.024 --> 01:00:19.029
Dr. Blake?


01:00:22.029 --> 01:00:22.712
Dr. Blake?


01:00:22.747 --> 01:00:23.396
Yes?


01:00:24.264 --> 01:00:27.968
Sorry about yesterday,
the Nixon girl.


01:00:28.003 --> 01:00:29.504
She seemed nice.


01:00:31.504 --> 01:00:34.212
She was.
Thank you.


01:00:39.211 --> 01:00:40.211
Dr. Blake?


01:00:40.246 --> 01:00:41.644
Yes?


01:00:41.679 --> 01:00:43.581
Dr. Waylans
would like to see you


01:00:43.616 --> 01:00:45.758
In conference room three.


01:00:53.757 --> 01:00:56.325
You wanted to see me?


01:00:56.360 --> 01:00:58.867
Yes, Martin.


01:00:58.902 --> 01:01:01.374
Take a seat.


01:01:10.373 --> 01:01:13.013
This the first time
this has happened?


01:01:18.012 --> 01:01:21.314
Yes.


01:01:21.349 --> 01:01:25.319
I never meant it to happen,
it just...


01:01:25.354 --> 01:01:30.130
got out of control.


01:01:37.129 --> 01:01:39.297
Well,
this is Dr. Sayler.


01:01:39.332 --> 01:01:42.100
She's a psychiatrist
on staff here.


01:01:42.135 --> 01:01:44.468
Hello, Martin.


01:01:44.503 --> 01:01:47.739
It's always hard
to lose a patient,


01:01:47.774 --> 01:01:50.307
Especially the first time.


01:01:50.342 --> 01:01:51.441
You always question yourself.


01:01:51.476 --> 01:01:55.578
You wonder if you made mistakes,
if you missed something,


01:01:55.613 --> 01:01:58.249
Could you have been quicker?


01:01:58.284 --> 01:02:00.415
These things happen.


01:02:00.450 --> 01:02:03.402
Accepting that
is part of being a doctor.


01:02:03.437 --> 01:02:06.356
If there's anything
you want to express,


01:02:06.391 --> 01:02:08.333
Please don't hold back.


01:02:17.332 --> 01:02:20.203
Can I ask you a question?


01:02:22.202 --> 01:02:23.435
Okay.


01:02:23.470 --> 01:02:26.309
Did you cry yesterday?


01:02:29.309 --> 01:02:32.480
I did, yes.


01:02:34.480 --> 01:02:37.416
Good.


01:02:37.451 --> 01:02:39.288
That's good.


01:02:41.287 --> 01:02:43.205
Oh, Mr. Nixon,
I am so sorr...


01:02:43.240 --> 01:02:45.124
Just want to talk
to the doctor.


01:02:46.124 --> 01:02:47.158
You killed my little girl.


01:02:47.193 --> 01:02:49.592
Okay, Mr. Nixon,
I am truly sorry for your loss,


01:02:49.627 --> 01:02:52.230
But you cannot come onto my ward
and start accusing my doctors.


01:02:52.265 --> 01:02:54.032
That bastard killed
my daughter.


01:02:54.067 --> 01:02:55.483
- Okay.
- What is the problem, sir?


01:02:55.518 --> 01:02:56.865
She was fine,
then she came in here,


01:02:56.900 --> 01:02:59.152
And you killed her.
- Martin, let me handle this.


01:02:59.187 --> 01:03:01.405
Sir, these infections can be
very difficult to treat.


01:03:01.440 --> 01:03:03.371
It was a rare,
resistant strain.


01:03:03.406 --> 01:03:05.758
Now, if she didn't take
every one of her pills,


01:03:05.793 --> 01:03:08.111
That could strengthen
the infection... We don't know.


01:03:08.146 --> 01:03:09.376
She tool her pills.
She told me.


01:03:09.411 --> 01:03:11.345
Don't blame dr. Blake, sir.
I supervised him


01:03:11.380 --> 01:03:15.418
Through the entire case.
He was exemplary in every way.


01:03:15.453 --> 01:03:16.286
We did everything we could,


01:03:17.286 --> 01:03:19.859
Everything, all of us.


01:03:24.859 --> 01:03:28.163
Sir, can you come with me,
please?


01:03:29.163 --> 01:03:32.768
Sir.
- Get your hands off me.


01:03:34.768 --> 01:03:37.272
You bastards.


01:03:39.272 --> 01:03:40.739
Is the situation under control,


01:03:40.774 --> 01:03:42.273
Or do you need backup?


01:03:42.308 --> 01:03:44.643
Everything's fine.
We're comin' out.


01:03:44.678 --> 01:03:46.642
I'm sorry, Martin.


01:03:46.677 --> 01:03:49.751
You shouldn't have to
deal with that.


01:03:53.751 --> 01:03:56.420
It's a tough one.


01:03:56.455 --> 01:03:58.320
Yeah.


01:03:58.355 --> 01:03:59.789
Don't worry about it.
Waylans told me


01:03:59.824 --> 01:04:03.319
You're not really a doctor
until you've lost a patient.


01:05:22.698 --> 01:05:25.803
You got your scrubs.


01:05:27.803 --> 01:05:29.710
Hey, hold up.


01:05:34.709 --> 01:05:36.943
Goin' to X-Ray,
Mr. Granger?


01:05:36.978 --> 01:05:38.843
There's no hearing aid.


01:05:38.878 --> 01:05:42.847
Right, Mr. Granger,
you crazy, old fucker?


01:05:42.882 --> 01:05:46.418
So it must be a relief
to get onto that new rotation.


01:05:46.453 --> 01:05:48.587
Sounds like that last one
was pretty rough.


01:05:48.622 --> 01:05:49.953
These things happen,
unfortunately.


01:05:49.988 --> 01:05:53.325
It's part of being a doctor,
dealing with loss.


01:05:53.360 --> 01:05:57.696
Oh.
So I guess you're a doctor now.


01:05:57.731 --> 01:05:59.362
I suppose so.


01:05:59.397 --> 01:06:01.331
You know what I always thought
would be the best part


01:06:01.366 --> 01:06:03.265
About being a doctor?


01:06:03.300 --> 01:06:08.372
It's the ladies.
The ladies love a doctor.


01:06:08.407 --> 01:06:09.573
You find that to be true?


01:06:09.608 --> 01:06:12.544
I suppose so, yes.


01:06:14.544 --> 01:06:16.613
No.
What do you mean?


01:06:18.681 --> 01:06:20.583
Meet me in the east tower
basement, five minutes.


01:06:20.618 --> 01:06:23.451
- Why?
- I think you know.


01:06:27.090 --> 01:06:28.255
What is it?


01:06:28.290 --> 01:06:31.392
Well, doctor, I just wanted to
ask you an ethical question


01:06:31.427 --> 01:06:34.579
About the relations
between staff and patients.


01:06:34.614 --> 01:06:37.731
That woman in the supply room?
Forget about it.


01:06:37.766 --> 01:06:39.265
No, no, no, no,
that's not my question.


01:06:39.300 --> 01:06:41.702
See, I'm more interested
in a situation like this.


01:06:41.737 --> 01:06:43.371
All right, say a guy like me,


01:06:43.406 --> 01:06:44.970
You know, who likes to party,


01:06:45.005 --> 01:06:47.790
But otherwise is a regular guy,
like an orderly,


01:06:47.825 --> 01:06:50.576
One day, he's takin' this gurney
to change it out...


01:06:50.611 --> 01:06:52.245
Oh, and the previous tenant
was this girl,


01:06:52.280 --> 01:06:54.831
It was a sweet girl,
she just passed away.


01:06:54.866 --> 01:06:57.381
Anyway, this guy's
takin' out the mattress,


01:06:57.416 --> 01:06:58.381
And to his surprise,


01:06:58.416 --> 01:07:00.017
Finds a little book
under there,


01:07:00.052 --> 01:07:04.523
And, well, there's some
really shocking stuff in there


01:07:04.558 --> 01:07:07.389
About this one young doctor.


01:07:07.424 --> 01:07:10.629
Seems they had kind of a little,
special relationship goin' on.


01:07:12.629 --> 01:07:16.566
Now my question is this,
do you think it's wrong,


01:07:16.601 --> 01:07:18.832
Ethically, for this orderly


01:07:18.867 --> 01:07:23.350
To keep this book
from his superiors?


01:07:34.348 --> 01:07:37.368
Let's take a ride.


01:07:55.234 --> 01:07:57.101
Another reason
I wish I was a doctor


01:07:57.136 --> 01:08:01.940
Is so I could prescribe myself
a better time.


01:08:01.975 --> 01:08:03.974
I party, and nobody sees this.


01:08:04.009 --> 01:08:05.642
I can't do that.


01:08:05.677 --> 01:08:08.742
Where there's a will,
there's a way, right?


01:08:38.739 --> 01:08:40.543
Ahem, doctor?


01:08:42.543 --> 01:08:45.146
Uh, I had a question
about this order.


01:08:45.181 --> 01:08:46.644
Is it my handwriting?


01:08:46.679 --> 01:08:48.847
Uh, no, I can read it,
it's just,


01:08:48.882 --> 01:08:51.715
You prescribed Oxycodone
for Mr. Granger?


01:08:51.750 --> 01:08:54.853
He's had some pain from
the hickman catheter, so yeah.


01:08:54.888 --> 01:08:59.195
Okay, sorry,
I just wanted to check.


01:09:04.195 --> 01:09:06.198
Do you need help?


01:09:06.233 --> 01:09:08.096
No, thanks.


01:09:08.131 --> 01:09:10.600
W- What's troubling you?


01:09:10.635 --> 01:09:11.633
What?


01:09:11.668 --> 01:09:13.668
That's for stomachs,


01:09:13.703 --> 01:09:17.174
And that stuff's more for,
like, sniffling and sneezing.


01:09:17.209 --> 01:09:19.776
I know.
I'm a doctor.


01:09:19.811 --> 01:09:23.055
Okay, sorry.


01:10:06.050 --> 01:10:08.751
Dude, four?


01:10:08.786 --> 01:10:10.120
They're hard to get.


01:10:10.155 --> 01:10:12.089
I hope this is a down payment.


01:10:12.124 --> 01:10:14.490
Okay, fine.


01:10:14.525 --> 01:10:16.010
What about the book?


01:10:16.045 --> 01:10:17.460
What about it?


01:10:17.495 --> 01:10:18.928
When do I get it back?


01:10:18.963 --> 01:10:21.729
You never had it.


01:10:21.764 --> 01:10:24.601
I'm not gonna do this
indefinitely.


01:10:25.901 --> 01:10:29.153
I don't think you have
much of a choice, doctor.


01:10:44.151 --> 01:10:48.089
Time you switched to decaf?


01:10:48.124 --> 01:10:50.233
Mmm.


01:11:05.738 --> 01:11:07.607
Cheers.


01:11:09.607 --> 01:11:11.641
Rotation wasn't so tough.


01:11:11.676 --> 01:11:13.144
And they say
the second half of the year,


01:11:13.179 --> 01:11:15.313
Everything gets easier.


01:11:15.348 --> 01:11:16.779
Martin.


01:11:16.814 --> 01:11:18.749
I'm sorry to hear about
your patient.


01:11:18.784 --> 01:11:21.283
Difficult case.
- Yes, it was.


01:11:21.318 --> 01:11:23.217
I've been doing a study
of these resistant bugs


01:11:23.252 --> 01:11:26.556
And was hoping you might be able
to help me review this one


01:11:26.591 --> 01:11:29.724
If you kept your notes
and charts together.


01:11:29.759 --> 01:11:31.561
Dr. Waylans tells me
you're thinking of applying


01:11:31.596 --> 01:11:32.928
For the I.D. Fellowship.


01:11:32.963 --> 01:11:34.261
Yes, I am.


01:11:34.296 --> 01:11:35.232
I think that's a fine idea.


01:11:36.232 --> 01:11:38.254
Fine idea.


01:12:33.248 --> 01:12:35.316
Yo, doc.
Is this the patient?


01:12:35.351 --> 01:12:37.251
Yes.


01:12:37.286 --> 01:12:39.119
James?
- Yeah?


01:12:39.154 --> 01:12:42.091
I'd like to talk to you,
when you get a chance.


01:12:42.126 --> 01:12:45.233
- Yeah, I get off in 30 minutes.
- Great.


01:12:52.233 --> 01:12:55.784
- Hello, doctor.
- Hi.


01:13:10.783 --> 01:13:13.020
Hey, there, partner.


01:13:14.019 --> 01:13:17.157
You got it?


01:13:19.157 --> 01:13:20.656
Those are different.


01:13:20.691 --> 01:13:23.009
They're more like morphine.


01:13:23.044 --> 01:13:25.328
They're better.
I want the book.


01:13:25.363 --> 01:13:27.997
Oh.
Maybe soon.


01:13:28.032 --> 01:13:30.231
Really?


01:13:30.266 --> 01:13:32.099
No,
that's not gonna work for me.


01:13:32.134 --> 01:13:35.438
You just keep 'em comin',
you'll be all right.


01:13:35.473 --> 01:13:37.138
Have fun.


01:13:37.173 --> 01:13:38.277
You know I will.


01:13:41.277 --> 01:13:43.277
What are you doing?
You can't take those here.


01:13:43.312 --> 01:13:45.344
Why not?
I'm off duty.


01:13:45.379 --> 01:13:47.115
You shouldn't drive on them.


01:13:47.150 --> 01:13:49.358
I got a ride.


01:13:57.357 --> 01:13:59.225
What's with you, man?


01:13:59.260 --> 01:14:01.927
Dude, don't make a big deal
out of this.


01:14:01.962 --> 01:14:03.127
We're all human beings.


01:14:03.162 --> 01:14:05.197
We all gotta get
our kicks somehow.


01:14:05.232 --> 01:14:07.233
What are you doing?
Don't follow me.


01:14:07.268 --> 01:14:08.789
I'm just walking.


01:14:08.824 --> 01:14:10.309
Get away from me.


01:14:17.309 --> 01:14:21.178
You're makin' this
more than it has to be, doc.


01:14:21.213 --> 01:14:22.711
You want more?
Yeah.


01:14:22.746 --> 01:14:24.315
- You want more?
- Sure, yeah.


01:14:24.350 --> 01:14:27.094
All right.


01:15:20.498 --> 01:15:21.301
Oof.


01:15:31.175 --> 01:15:33.778
- What's goin' on?
- I don't know.


01:15:33.813 --> 01:15:35.210
Some kind of seizure.


01:15:35.245 --> 01:15:36.510
Call a code,
he's gone into arrest!


01:15:36.545 --> 01:15:38.180
All right, all right,
I got it. I'm on it. Okay.


01:15:38.182 --> 01:15:38.215
Okay, jimmy!


01:15:39.182 --> 01:15:41.267
Jimmy, can you hear me?
Jimmy?


01:15:41.302 --> 01:15:43.394
Okay, okay, okay.


01:15:43.429 --> 01:15:45.625
Jimmy, it's dr. Waylans.
Jimmy!


01:15:45.660 --> 01:15:47.822
Jimmy, stay with me.


01:15:47.857 --> 01:15:51.146
Jimmy.
Stay with us.


01:16:44.140 --> 01:16:47.208
- So was he sick or anything?
- I don't know.


01:16:47.243 --> 01:16:50.210
He went into some kind of
seizure. I tried to help.


01:16:50.245 --> 01:16:52.948
I wouldn't be surprised if it
was some sort of drug overdose.


01:16:52.983 --> 01:16:54.666
What makes you think that?


01:16:54.701 --> 01:16:56.315
It's very erratic behavior.


01:16:56.350 --> 01:16:58.252
Some of the nursing staff,
it occurred to them


01:16:58.287 --> 01:16:59.918
That he might be a drug abuser.


01:16:59.953 --> 01:17:01.524
They had
a mandatory test scheduled.


01:17:04.524 --> 01:17:06.193
Perhaps you should go home.
Take a break.


01:17:07.193 --> 01:17:09.162
Get back to the business
of being a doctor on monday.


01:17:09.197 --> 01:17:11.263
You off tomorrow?


01:17:11.298 --> 01:17:13.598
Yup.


01:17:13.633 --> 01:17:15.032
Okay with you, detective,


01:17:15.067 --> 01:17:16.468
If the good doctor here
goes home?


01:17:16.503 --> 01:17:19.570
Uh...yeah, I guess.


01:17:19.605 --> 01:17:22.274
If we have any more questions,
we'll be in touch,


01:17:22.309 --> 01:17:24.664
If you don't mind.


01:17:24.699 --> 01:17:27.020
No, not at all.


01:17:35.019 --> 01:17:36.252
He kissed me...


01:17:36.287 --> 01:17:39.022
went to the hospital today...
they want to keep me overnight.


01:17:39.057 --> 01:17:40.322
Rich asked me to be
his girlfriend...


01:17:40.357 --> 01:17:44.310
the diagnosis is...
...but he doesn't act like it...


01:17:44.345 --> 01:17:47.371
looks like a U.T.I... If you
love someone, set them free.


01:17:47.406 --> 01:17:50.398
I spent the night at rich's...
they called a specialist.


01:17:50.433 --> 01:17:52.902
He carried me into the bedroom
and laid me down...


01:17:52.937 --> 01:17:56.370
I can't believe he's...
he's such a liar.


01:17:56.405 --> 01:17:59.374
Having surgery tomorrow...
I have a step-Sister...


01:17:59.409 --> 01:18:01.174
they put the tube in
this morning...


01:18:01.209 --> 01:18:03.327
it's an infection.
The anesthesia was great...


01:18:03.362 --> 01:18:05.446
it's actually...
gave me the weirdest dreams...


01:18:30.035 --> 01:18:31.536
Dr. Blake?


01:18:31.571 --> 01:18:33.202
Yes.


01:18:33.237 --> 01:18:36.373
Detective Krauss,
from the hospital yesterday.


01:18:36.408 --> 01:18:38.692
You said
if we had any more questions...


01:18:38.727 --> 01:18:40.977
I'm sorry
to just drop by like this.


01:18:41.012 --> 01:18:44.579
Right.
Fine, come in.


01:19:02.530 --> 01:19:04.297
Can I get you anything?


01:19:04.332 --> 01:19:06.966
No, thanks.


01:19:07.001 --> 01:19:10.337
So it seems the, uh,
the pills Mr. Vega took


01:19:10.372 --> 01:19:13.205
Were spiked
with potassium cyanide.


01:19:13.240 --> 01:19:16.974
You know about that?
- No.


01:19:17.009 --> 01:19:21.179
Well, yeah, I mean,
I know what it is.


01:19:21.214 --> 01:19:24.482
Some people suspect that he,
uh, he abused drugs.


01:19:24.517 --> 01:19:27.018
Looks like
maybe he got a bad batch.


01:19:27.053 --> 01:19:29.255
That's a shame.


01:19:31.254 --> 01:19:33.222
I mean,
I didn't know him that well.


01:19:33.257 --> 01:19:37.361
That's why I'm not as upset as
I would be if I knew him better.


01:19:37.396 --> 01:19:41.229
I knew him to say hello to.


01:19:41.264 --> 01:19:42.698
Did you ever see him
taking drugs?


01:19:42.733 --> 01:19:44.333
No.


01:19:44.368 --> 01:19:47.742
I hardly knew him, like I said.


01:20:04.251 --> 01:20:06.593
You have a pen I could borrow?


01:20:12.592 --> 01:20:14.296
Thanks.


01:20:16.296 --> 01:20:19.096
You knew this, uh, orderly.


01:20:19.131 --> 01:20:24.068
Just slightly.
Not well, kind of.


01:20:24.103 --> 01:20:26.139
I mean, he was...
not my kind of person.


01:20:26.174 --> 01:20:28.174
Do you know
where he got the drugs?


01:20:29.174 --> 01:20:31.343
Could he have gotten them
from the hospital, stolen them?


01:20:31.378 --> 01:20:32.794
No, they're
carefully monitored,


01:20:32.829 --> 01:20:34.211
So I don't know
how an orderly could.


01:20:34.246 --> 01:20:36.250
Only a doctor can prescribe.


01:20:38.249 --> 01:20:42.219
Could a doctor have
gotten them for him?


01:20:42.254 --> 01:20:45.256
Theoretically...
a doctor could...


01:20:45.291 --> 01:20:47.791
fake a prescription,
or skim from a patient,


01:20:47.826 --> 01:20:50.293
But that wouldn't be ethical,
so they don't.


01:20:50.328 --> 01:20:53.334
So a doctor
could have gotten these.


01:20:59.333 --> 01:21:01.301
No.


01:21:01.336 --> 01:21:04.573
Did any doctors have any kind
of a relationship with Mr. Vega?


01:21:04.608 --> 01:21:06.605
What? No, I...
I don't know.


01:21:06.640 --> 01:21:08.242
I mean, like I said,
I didn't care for him,


01:21:08.277 --> 01:21:09.408
So I didn't hang around him.


01:21:09.443 --> 01:21:13.281
Were there any other doctors
who may have disliked him,


01:21:13.316 --> 01:21:18.350
Who could've tainted the pills
with the, uh, the...


01:21:18.385 --> 01:21:21.392
Potassium cyanide.


01:21:25.391 --> 01:21:27.876
Look, uh...


01:21:27.911 --> 01:21:30.361
I'm sorry if I seem distracted.


01:21:30.396 --> 01:21:34.263
I understand.


01:21:34.298 --> 01:21:35.833
It must be tough
trying to get back to normal,


01:21:35.868 --> 01:21:38.539
After seeing somebody
die like that.


01:21:42.539 --> 01:21:45.442
It has been...


01:21:45.477 --> 01:21:48.346
especially with her.


01:21:50.346 --> 01:21:51.551
Who?


01:21:54.550 --> 01:21:58.351
No one.


01:21:58.386 --> 01:22:00.520
Just...
A patient died.


01:22:00.555 --> 01:22:03.941
It was a resistant strain
of an infection.


01:22:03.976 --> 01:22:07.294
They're rare,
but increasingly common.


01:22:07.329 --> 01:22:11.232
Antibiotics and cleansers
are making germs tougher.


01:22:11.267 --> 01:22:14.204
It was a difficult case,
everyone agreed.


01:22:17.204 --> 01:22:19.271
I know I must seem like
I'm reacting differently now


01:22:19.306 --> 01:22:22.175
Than with james' passing away,
but he wasn't much of a person.


01:22:22.210 --> 01:22:24.211
I mean, he'd make
lewd comments at women patients.


01:22:24.246 --> 01:22:26.212
I think he may have even
fooled around with them,


01:22:26.247 --> 01:22:27.819
Which, as a doctor, you can't.


01:22:32.818 --> 01:22:35.653
Diane was a very nice girl.


01:22:35.688 --> 01:22:37.488
We were close.


01:22:37.523 --> 01:22:40.228
In a doctor-Patient way,
before she died...


01:22:44.228 --> 01:22:45.760
but that's over now,


01:22:45.795 --> 01:22:48.166
And I'm back to
the business of being a doctor.


01:22:49.166 --> 01:22:50.335
Beautiful day, isn't it?


01:22:53.335 --> 01:22:55.638
Well, you know where I am,
detective,


01:22:55.673 --> 01:22:58.717
If you have any more questions.


01:23:13.488 --> 01:23:16.341
Excuse me a moment.


01:23:33.339 --> 01:23:34.371
Doctor?


01:23:34.406 --> 01:23:36.307
Just a second.


01:23:36.342 --> 01:23:38.574
Mind if I have
a glass of water?


01:23:38.609 --> 01:23:40.808
No, not at all.
Help yourself.


01:26:28.762 --> 01:26:29.962
I'm sorry.


01:26:29.997 --> 01:26:32.798
I need to collect some things.
I'm needed at the hospital.


01:26:32.833 --> 01:26:34.367
Do you have any more questions?


01:26:34.402 --> 01:26:35.901
I'm afraid
I'm in a bit of a hurry.


01:26:35.936 --> 01:26:38.504
Well, no.


01:26:38.539 --> 01:26:41.038
I guess not.


01:26:41.073 --> 01:26:43.484
I'll let you get ready, then.


01:26:51.483 --> 01:26:53.016
Thanks for your help, doctor.


01:26:53.051 --> 01:26:54.395
My pleasure.


01:27:12.634 --> 01:27:14.785
His h&h are 12 and 36.
WBC 10.9


01:27:14.820 --> 01:27:16.813
With a slight shift
to the left.


01:27:16.848 --> 01:27:18.461
He's on a broad-Spectrum
antibiotic.


01:27:18.496 --> 01:27:20.039
I'm about to hang
his third dose.


01:27:20.074 --> 01:27:22.010
- Let's do blood cultures now
and times two for a temporary,


01:27:22.045 --> 01:27:23.043
Then 101.
- Yeah.


01:27:23.078 --> 01:27:25.113
- Is it gonna hurt?
- A little, but don't worry.


01:27:26.113 --> 01:27:28.015
I'm getting better all the time.
Make a fist.


01:27:28.050 --> 01:27:29.819
- Doctor?
- Yes.

